                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f23a7647-61f6-3c47-9ae4-7d6349bda662",
                        "entry_id": "d445dbce-c483-37fa-8b28-e604927fdac0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "клятвенное обещание не делать чего-либо, делать что-либо, зарок"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5e10d6f7-4602-4412-8f6e-590a657a98a8",
                                "sense_id": "f23a7647-61f6-3c47-9ae4-7d6349bda662",
                                "text": "Кыскин делал новые уверения, давал новые заклятия и зароки, а через год снова плелся отыскивать кума и куму."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f0f65ea1-4e3c-365b-a50a-83681d4adfce",
                        "entry_id": "d445dbce-c483-37fa-8b28-e604927fdac0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "колдовство, приводящее к магическому изменению естественного хода событий"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b8cdf54e-4a19-4a3f-8e02-b8eef0134bc3",
                                "sense_id": "f0f65ea1-4e3c-365b-a50a-83681d4adfce",
                                "text": "Злая волшебница прогневалась на моего родителя покойного, короля славного и могучего, украла меня, ещё малолетнего, и сатанинским колдовством своим, силой нечистою, оборотила меня в чудище страшное и наложила таковое заклятие, чтобы жить мне в таковом виде безобразном, противном и страшном для всякого человека, для всякой твари божией, пока найдётся красная девица, какого бы роду и званья ни была она, и полюбит меня в образе страшилища, и пожелает быть моей женой законною, и тогда колдовство всё покончится, и стану я опять по-прежнему человеком молодым и пригожиим; и жил я таковым страшилищем и пугалом ровно тридцать лет, и залучал я в мой дворец заколдованный одиннадцать девиц красных, а ты была двенадцатая."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1cdc62c0-9673-37f2-a3cb-a1e90c16c492",
                        "entry_id": "d445dbce-c483-37fa-8b28-e604927fdac0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "волшебное высказывание, приводящее к магическому изменению естественного хода событий"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9a6e6e09-33c7-4919-8651-3e1ddf7a7397",
                                "sense_id": "1cdc62c0-9673-37f2-a3cb-a1e90c16c492",
                                "text": "Конечно, из-за трудности ловли этого зверя держится на Севере поверье, что против лисицы надобно знать слово, т. е. заклятие: «Иной, ― говорят, ― как ни изворачивается, ни старается, не может уловить ни одной», ― этот иной, конечно, только более неосторожен и менее умен, чем лисица."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "39d71a9d-87b2-4273-9896-16add8209ef1",
                        "source_entry_id": "d445dbce-c483-37fa-8b28-e604927fdac0",
                        "target_lang_word": "spell",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "spell",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "21aef9a2-0616-3527-a2a6-d2cff67e76bd",
                                        "entry_id": "ec6d839c-c701-3e4b-8e91-0ec7cc48bf49",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Words or a formula supposed to have magical powers."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "16d4bbf0-0e99-4ec2-ba12-2c4012d1d250",
                                                "sense_id": "21aef9a2-0616-3527-a2a6-d2cff67e76bd",
                                                "text": "He cast a spell to cure warts."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8e06e216-45fb-3691-a2b0-1cbd2ad29e26",
                                        "entry_id": "ec6d839c-c701-3e4b-8e91-0ec7cc48bf49",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A magical effect or influence induced by an incantation or formula."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2044c439-dd4e-41e7-98af-1338d78d43c3",
                                                "sense_id": "8e06e216-45fb-3691-a2b0-1cbd2ad29e26",
                                                "text": "under a spell"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "018f6dd3-e9b2-4c27-9e82-29c09f3ef3e7",
                                                "sense_id": "8e06e216-45fb-3691-a2b0-1cbd2ad29e26",
                                                "text": "Skies are not so black / Mary took me back / Mary has broken your spell"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f241772-c012-47f2-b8bf-b7332d8d424c",
                                                "sense_id": "8e06e216-45fb-3691-a2b0-1cbd2ad29e26",
                                                "text": "I believe your love has placed its spell on me"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "647c6615-9dbe-3967-8f9f-218c9089365e",
                                        "entry_id": "ec6d839c-c701-3e4b-8e91-0ec7cc48bf49",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Speech, discourse."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "spell",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6f6205b8-17df-3576-9b6f-eea724861653",
                                        "entry_id": "e78f6e69-068a-3de2-bc1d-8eeb0471cc79",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To put under the influence of a spell; to affect by a spell; to bewitch; to fascinate; to charm."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "23bdc3fe-074f-4d0d-af94-30463105e7a9",
                                                "sense_id": "6f6205b8-17df-3576-9b6f-eea724861653",
                                                "text": "Vnchaine your spirits now with spelling Charmes,"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f4105f90-e4a7-4676-a28b-20ff457ac809",
                                                "sense_id": "6f6205b8-17df-3576-9b6f-eea724861653",
                                                "text": "[…] although the Kings Jealousie was thus particular to her, his Affection was as general to others […] Above all, for a time he was much speld with Elianor Talbot […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f48e0031-5934-4c61-b8e2-9fbc164dc40d",
                                                "sense_id": "6f6205b8-17df-3576-9b6f-eea724861653",
                                                "text": "1697, John Dryden (translator), Georgics, Book 3 in The Works of Virgil, London: Jacob Tonson, p. 109, lines 444-446,\nThis, gather’d in the Planetary Hour,\nWith noxious Weeds, and spell’d with Words of pow’r\nDire Stepdames in the Magick Bowl infuse;"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "87e7ba6d-b460-413a-bc9f-f13cf76358cc",
                                                "sense_id": "6f6205b8-17df-3576-9b6f-eea724861653",
                                                "text": "But when, O Wells! thy roses came to me\nMy sense with their deliciousness was spell’d:"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "spell",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3e18b417-6568-3696-92e2-eea1bf3ade91",
                                        "entry_id": "867d7ba1-fe11-3de6-94ad-eeb27e2c088d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To write or say the letters that form a word or part of a word."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "sometimes",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57767ca5-3681-4ae7-84fd-cac60bbb7b7b",
                                                "sense_id": "3e18b417-6568-3696-92e2-eea1bf3ade91",
                                                "text": "I find it difficult to spell because I'm dyslexic."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8cc7cdf1-d1ad-3fec-b10a-4b0294bbaafd",
                                        "entry_id": "867d7ba1-fe11-3de6-94ad-eeb27e2c088d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To read (something) as though letter by letter; to peruse slowly or with effort."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae73ade1-badc-4062-bc39-cd30094817d5",
                                                "sense_id": "8cc7cdf1-d1ad-3fec-b10a-4b0294bbaafd",
                                                "text": "\"He'll do,\" said Bildad, eyeing me, and then went on spelling away at his book in a mumbling tone quite audible."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "79d50bed-8685-34d7-a338-7ffd3eb87d2b",
                                        "entry_id": "867d7ba1-fe11-3de6-94ad-eeb27e2c088d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of letters: to compose (a word)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "528d5906-1b01-4740-9443-07a257421660",
                                                "sense_id": "79d50bed-8685-34d7-a338-7ffd3eb87d2b",
                                                "text": "The letters “a”, “n” and “d” spell “and”."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "23e4d613-f78c-470b-8846-5d81e4143652",
                                                "sense_id": "79d50bed-8685-34d7-a338-7ffd3eb87d2b",
                                                "text": "In Esperanto each letter has only one sound, and each sound is represented in only one way. The words are pronounced exactly as spelt, every letter being sounded."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "592355e7-f0a5-496c-9c19-eea2665c76db",
                                                "sense_id": "79d50bed-8685-34d7-a338-7ffd3eb87d2b",
                                                "text": "Welcome to the League Aiming to Menace and Overthrow Spies!\nYou realize that spells “LAMOS”?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "df2463f4-e087-3ac3-a3df-9905f0a5c94d",
                                        "entry_id": "867d7ba1-fe11-3de6-94ad-eeb27e2c088d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To clarify; to explain in detail."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b15fcf52-9788-4d2d-95a5-8443a9c03d2a",
                                                "sense_id": "df2463f4-e087-3ac3-a3df-9905f0a5c94d",
                                                "text": "Please spell it out for me."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea51bceb-028f-4e7e-9448-7b1a9d0fce88",
                                                "sense_id": "df2463f4-e087-3ac3-a3df-9905f0a5c94d",
                                                "text": "When we get elected, for instance, we get one of these, and we are pretty much told what is in it, and it is our responsibility to read it and understand it, and if we do not, the Ethics Committee, we can call them any time of day and ask them to spell it out for us[…]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bd3e1509-a1d0-3ab7-8dda-484a77a1ae77",
                                        "entry_id": "867d7ba1-fe11-3de6-94ad-eeb27e2c088d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To indicate that (some event) will occur; typically followed by a single-word noun."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a4a55c60-e588-40ef-855a-0b650d47bb38",
                                                "sense_id": "bd3e1509-a1d0-3ab7-8dda-484a77a1ae77",
                                                "text": "This spells trouble."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "63b2bb38-9485-3259-b33e-9810f5591de3",
                                        "entry_id": "867d7ba1-fe11-3de6-94ad-eeb27e2c088d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To constitute; to measure."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57784a94-c511-466a-9859-34c897c9ff1e",
                                                "sense_id": "63b2bb38-9485-3259-b33e-9810f5591de3",
                                                "text": "the Saxon heptarchy, when seven kings put together did spell but one in effect"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0be71c21-702e-317c-bf02-8791634805ae",
                                        "entry_id": "867d7ba1-fe11-3de6-94ad-eeb27e2c088d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To speak, to declaim."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "62851a5c-acd0-4b91-96a5-14c6ba2673ae",
                                                "sense_id": "0be71c21-702e-317c-bf02-8791634805ae",
                                                "text": "O who can tell / The hidden power of herbes, and might of Magicke spell?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dfbecea2-9dcc-3b6c-b8c0-804572721d92",
                                        "entry_id": "867d7ba1-fe11-3de6-94ad-eeb27e2c088d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To tell; to relate; to teach."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a022192f-f4c5-444e-9d5f-701aa101411c",
                                                "sense_id": "dfbecea2-9dcc-3b6c-b8c0-804572721d92",
                                                "text": "1770, Thomas Warton, “Ode on the Approach of Summer” in A Collection of Poems in Four Volumes, London: G. Pearch, Volume 1, p. 278,\nAs thro’ the caverns dim I wind,\nMight I that legend find,\nBy fairies spelt in mystic rhymes,"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "spell",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
